WEBVTT

00:26.420 --> 00:27.280
I'm Teika.

00:27.810 --> 00:29.040
I'm Yoritsuna.

00:29.550 --> 00:32.420
Thank you for coming to this performance

00:32.420 --> 00:34.430
by the Heian Ballet Company!

00:35.000 --> 00:36.370
By the way, Teika-kun...

00:36.370 --> 00:39.320
The Hyakunin Shuka, which
is said to be the basis

00:36.720 --> 00:43.730
Hyakunin Shuka

00:39.300 --> 00:40.870
for the Hyakunin Isshu,

00:40.870 --> 00:43.730
contains a poem by Empress Teishi, yes?

00:43.730 --> 00:45.520
Yes, that's right.

00:45.970 --> 00:48.850
Why wasn't it included
in the Hyakunin Isshu?

00:48.850 --> 00:50.730
It's a good poem.

00:53.420 --> 00:55.590
Yes, I wonder why.

02:27.130 --> 02:28.250
Tomorrow is the day?

02:28.590 --> 02:33.070
Yes, I'll be off to Mutsu
to spread my wings.

02:33.070 --> 02:34.470
I wonder how many ladies

02:34.470 --> 02:37.260
will be weeping over
your departure, Sanekata.

02:38.640 --> 02:40.250
I hope you're right.

02:42.040 --> 02:44.260
One regret would be that

02:44.260 --> 02:48.100
I will leave before I can
see that bud blossom.

02:49.130 --> 02:50.790
You mean Shonagon?

02:51.640 --> 02:53.790
Kinto, could you send her

02:53.790 --> 02:55.940
a letter or two, when you have time?

02:57.240 --> 02:59.870
Her reputation will
improve if she composes

02:59.870 --> 03:03.400
a reply that's worthy of you.

03:04.070 --> 03:08.410
And if she doesn't, your
ex will embarrass herself.

03:09.060 --> 03:11.620
It'll be fine.  She can handle it.

03:12.050 --> 03:14.080
Then I won't go easy on her.

03:14.080 --> 03:16.630
I'm eager to see what happens.

03:18.710 --> 03:21.800
However, Sanekata never
returned to the capital.

03:22.380 --> 03:25.420
A few years later,
towards the end of last year,

03:25.420 --> 03:28.040
he died in an accident.

03:29.810 --> 03:32.810
Nakoso Falls

03:29.810 --> 03:32.810
Dainagon Kinto

03:34.350 --> 03:36.980
I noticed how cold it was this morning.

03:40.220 --> 03:42.010
The last snow?

03:46.930 --> 03:50.800
Could you send her a letter
or two when you have time?

03:59.350 --> 04:00.630
Oh, it's so cold.

04:00.990 --> 04:03.620
Teishi-sama, you'll ruin your health

04:03.620 --> 04:06.580
if you spend too much time
gazing at the snow.

04:06.580 --> 04:08.970
Oh?  You're using me as an excuse

04:08.970 --> 04:11.010
to get yourselves out of the cold?

04:11.010 --> 04:12.680
No, that's not it.

04:12.680 --> 04:15.770
I'm worried about your health.

04:17.480 --> 04:19.570
Shonagon, that's enough.

04:19.570 --> 04:21.270
Please lower the curtain.

04:21.270 --> 04:22.870
Yes, Teishi-sama.

04:23.790 --> 04:27.570
So much has happened
to make me depressed,

04:27.570 --> 04:30.490
but I feel better now.

04:30.490 --> 04:34.270
I feel a little chilly now, though.

04:39.270 --> 04:41.170
It's so cold.

04:42.570 --> 04:44.430
Are you Shonagon?

04:44.430 --> 04:45.680
Yes.

04:45.680 --> 04:48.320
I have a letter from
Prime Minister Kinto.

04:48.320 --> 04:50.140
What?  Kinto-sama?

04:52.000 --> 04:55.120
Why would he send a letter to me?

04:56.350 --> 04:59.300
For but a moment,
I feel the coming of spring.

05:00.030 --> 05:02.100
Is this the second verse of a poem?

05:02.100 --> 05:05.320
He wants me to compose the first verse?

05:06.200 --> 05:08.010
Kinto-sama and the other court members

05:08.010 --> 05:09.490
await your response.

05:09.490 --> 05:10.420
What?

05:11.620 --> 05:15.860
I wonder how Sei Shonagon will respond.

05:15.860 --> 05:20.000
Wouldn't you say that this
is too difficult for her?

05:20.520 --> 05:22.250
I wouldn't know about that.

05:24.810 --> 05:26.360
I don't want to send

05:26.360 --> 05:28.190
Kinto-sama a response that's no good.

05:28.640 --> 05:30.560
I would ask Teishi-sama for advice,

05:30.560 --> 05:32.680
but the Emperor is currently visiting.

05:34.360 --> 05:36.340
I have come for your reply.

05:36.340 --> 05:38.930
Oh, what do I do?

05:39.450 --> 05:41.320
Please wait one moment.

05:41.320 --> 05:41.940
Yes.

05:42.850 --> 05:44.700
I definitely don't want to send

05:44.700 --> 05:46.630
a response that's bad and<i> late.</i>

05:52.840 --> 05:58.010
Snow falls like flower petals
from the wintry sky.

05:59.300 --> 06:00.780
On this cold morning,

06:00.780 --> 06:03.120
I gaze upon the snowfall as I would

06:03.120 --> 06:05.000
watch flower petals fall.

06:05.950 --> 06:09.130
For but a moment,
I feel the coming of spring.

06:10.240 --> 06:13.120
It seems there are signs of spring in the air.

06:14.530 --> 06:16.260
Shonagon amazes again!

06:16.260 --> 06:20.110
We should ask the Emperor
to bestow a title upon her.

06:21.610 --> 06:24.190
So you liked it?

06:24.680 --> 06:26.690
Yes, it was excellent.

06:27.340 --> 06:30.010
You were speaking of spring
on a snowy morning.

06:30.010 --> 06:31.750
That gave me the hint I needed.

06:32.420 --> 06:33.560
Your second verse was derived

06:33.560 --> 06:35.410
from Bai Juyi's "Southern Snow."

06:35.410 --> 06:36.240
Yes.

06:37.050 --> 06:41.110
Three in the morning,
snow in the cold air,

06:41.110 --> 06:44.650
February, in the chill of the mountains,
I feel the coming of spring.

06:45.560 --> 06:47.100
You're right.

06:47.100 --> 06:49.340
My second verse was based

06:49.340 --> 06:52.550
on his second verse about spring.

06:53.250 --> 06:56.310
So I based my first verse

06:56.310 --> 06:58.310
on his first verse about snow.

06:59.250 --> 07:01.120
And you compared
the snow to flower petals

07:01.120 --> 07:03.260
to invoke an image of spring.

07:04.170 --> 07:07.670
It seems that this riddle
was too easy for you.

07:07.670 --> 07:09.840
After all, Bai Juyi is...

07:09.840 --> 07:11.780
Basic reading?

07:11.780 --> 07:12.650
Huh?

07:12.650 --> 07:14.840
Someone once told me about

07:14.840 --> 07:17.410
a cheeky and talented girl

07:17.410 --> 07:20.630
who said that Bai Juyi
was basic reading.

07:21.840 --> 07:26.250
I love how you make witty
and cheeky comments.

07:26.750 --> 07:28.970
Was it Sanekata-sama?

07:30.380 --> 07:34.090
He always sounded so proud
when he spoke of you.

07:34.090 --> 07:36.220
He was always very concerned about you.

07:37.570 --> 07:39.600
Really...

07:42.280 --> 07:43.720
It's funny.

07:43.720 --> 07:46.150
Perhaps it's because he
told me so much about you,

07:46.150 --> 07:50.820
but it almost feels
like we're old friends.

07:50.820 --> 07:55.040
He told me a great deal
about you, Kinto-sama.

07:55.040 --> 07:55.990
Oh?

07:56.980 --> 07:58.390
He sounded so happy

07:58.390 --> 08:01.110
when he told me that
your coming-of-age ceremony

08:01.110 --> 08:04.520
would be held in the
presence of the Emperor.

08:05.250 --> 08:10.300
I feel like I've known
you for a long time, too.

08:12.720 --> 08:13.970
Sanekata...

08:15.050 --> 08:19.350
If only you were here.

08:26.270 --> 08:30.280
In the Kounin era, this place
was supposed to be beautiful,

08:30.280 --> 08:33.560
but a waterfall with no water is dead.

08:34.960 --> 08:38.070
Sanekata was once the
darling of the palace,

08:38.070 --> 08:40.490
but his name is no longer mentioned.

08:40.990 --> 08:43.630
I will also be a person
of the past, soon.

08:44.370 --> 08:45.420
Kinto!

08:46.740 --> 08:48.370
You need something, Michinaga-sama?

08:48.370 --> 08:51.910
Why do you look so bored
with this gathering?

08:51.910 --> 08:54.080
Because I'm bored.

08:54.080 --> 08:57.900
A waterfall viewing point with
no waterfall is meaningless.

08:59.040 --> 09:00.330
You have a point.

09:00.800 --> 09:02.830
How about a poem to lament

09:02.830 --> 09:04.490
the tragedy of this waterfall?

09:04.490 --> 09:06.090
Yes.

09:06.090 --> 09:08.060
Could you give me some time?

09:08.920 --> 09:12.320
Yukinari, you should
compose a poem as well.

09:12.320 --> 09:13.130
No,

09:13.750 --> 09:16.570
my role is to write down
the poems you compose.

09:17.920 --> 09:20.950
Since you have the best
handwriting in the world.

09:20.950 --> 09:23.510
Very well.  Let us know
when you're finished.

09:24.540 --> 09:25.760
Yes, yes.

09:26.880 --> 09:28.150
Say, Yukinari.

09:28.150 --> 09:31.080
Am I such an easy read?

09:31.080 --> 09:34.670
You look much more bored than I do.

09:34.670 --> 09:36.600
I always look bored.

09:36.600 --> 09:37.780
Lucky you.

09:37.780 --> 09:40.300
Then, I should practice that look.

09:41.380 --> 09:43.680
Still, Michinaga is quite peculiar.

09:44.360 --> 09:46.860
He's skipping the council
to see the scenery.

09:47.320 --> 09:51.320
We're also guilty of the same offense.

09:51.320 --> 09:53.660
We aren't blameless,

09:53.660 --> 09:55.570
but this is mainly the Emperor's fault.

09:56.340 --> 09:59.950
He refuses to wed Michinaga's daughter.

09:59.950 --> 10:01.720
Though it's immature of Michinaga

10:01.720 --> 10:04.120
to skip the council because of that.

10:04.890 --> 10:08.530
However, he's the only man who can lead

10:08.530 --> 10:10.280
the council right now.

10:10.280 --> 10:12.730
The Emperor needs to compromise

10:12.730 --> 10:14.520
or the government will come to a halt.

10:15.090 --> 10:17.720
The Emperor must know that.

10:18.270 --> 10:22.000
The Emperor is doing this
to protect Teishi-sama.

10:22.610 --> 10:24.500
Because her position is perilous

10:24.500 --> 10:27.230
now that she has no one to back her.

10:27.850 --> 10:29.440
A touching tale, but personal matters

10:29.440 --> 10:31.230
have no place in government.

10:32.140 --> 10:35.900
It's your duty as Head
Chamberlain to make that clear.

10:37.430 --> 10:39.150
You're just like the Emperor.

10:40.050 --> 10:42.890
Are you hesitant because
there's someone you

10:42.890 --> 10:44.490
care about in the Empress' camp?

10:46.920 --> 10:49.310
Don't mix private affairs with work.

10:49.310 --> 10:51.020
When forced to choose between

10:51.020 --> 10:54.260
your job and your friends,
you must give up one of the two.

10:55.490 --> 10:56.630
I know.

10:59.210 --> 11:00.380
Okay, I got it.

11:01.110 --> 11:02.730
I'll recite the poem,
so write it down.

11:02.730 --> 11:03.720
Oh, yes.

11:04.760 --> 11:09.350
No more can we hear the
sounds of the waterfall,

11:09.350 --> 11:12.740
but its legacy continues to spread.

11:13.690 --> 11:17.590
We can no longer hear the sounds of the

11:17.590 --> 11:19.890
magnificent waterfall
which once stood here,

11:19.890 --> 11:23.300
but its name is still
spoken of to this day.

11:24.710 --> 11:26.680
Good, not too bad.

11:27.250 --> 11:28.190
Kinto-sama.

11:29.520 --> 11:31.870
Do you truly believe our
names will be remembered?

11:32.840 --> 11:35.070
Glory is as short-lived as a dream.

11:35.720 --> 11:38.510
We struggle now to
accomplish great things,

11:38.960 --> 11:43.550
but eventually, no one will
know that we ever lived.

11:44.990 --> 11:46.220
I suppose.

11:46.850 --> 11:49.360
After seeing other people fade away,

11:49.360 --> 11:50.940
I have to agree.

11:51.480 --> 11:53.440
However, there is hope.

11:53.680 --> 11:56.880
My poems and my friends'
poems, your books,

11:56.880 --> 11:59.190
and your friends' writings.

11:59.440 --> 12:01.450
These may last forever.

12:02.200 --> 12:04.130
In any case,

12:04.840 --> 12:06.890
we have no way of knowing the future,

12:06.890 --> 12:09.660
so we can only go with the flow

12:09.660 --> 12:16.310
and try our best to survive
in this unpredictable world.

12:25.190 --> 12:27.430
Teishi-sama has been
named Empress Consort,

12:27.430 --> 12:30.000
while Shoshi-sama has
become the new Empress.

12:30.710 --> 12:33.230
The Emperor now has two first wives.

12:33.230 --> 12:35.980
Michinaga-sama is being reckless.

12:36.560 --> 12:41.610
Yukinari-sama was the one
who convinced the Emperor.

12:48.600 --> 12:49.690
I must...

12:50.460 --> 12:54.280
I must protect Teishi-sama,
no matter what happens.

12:58.310 --> 13:01.590
Teishi-sama, I've brought some melon
that was delivered this morning.

13:02.680 --> 13:03.950
Shonagon...

13:04.510 --> 13:06.260
It's quite refreshing.

13:06.670 --> 13:10.930
You must eat enough for
the child you carry.

13:11.520 --> 13:13.230
Yes, I know.

13:14.020 --> 13:17.480
Choho 2, December 16

13:18.290 --> 13:19.590
I bring news!

13:20.460 --> 13:22.280
The Emperor has an heir.

13:22.280 --> 13:23.480
After Teishi-sama...

13:23.480 --> 13:25.860
After Teishi-sama gave birth to a son,

13:26.730 --> 13:28.370
she passed away.

13:46.390 --> 13:47.410
Yukinari-sama.

13:48.770 --> 13:50.670
Aren't you supposed to meet with

13:50.670 --> 13:51.950
the ministers this afternoon?

13:51.950 --> 13:53.960
Yes, I'll leave now.

13:56.360 --> 13:58.320
I won't be returning today.

13:58.320 --> 14:00.710
If anything comes up, send a runner.

14:00.710 --> 14:01.570
Yes.

14:02.960 --> 14:06.080
Yukinari-sama seems to
have lost his cheer.

14:06.080 --> 14:07.740
You can't blame him.

14:07.740 --> 14:11.450
His request for a promotion
was rejected again.

14:11.450 --> 14:14.730
Ah...  The position of Head
Chamberlain is difficult to fill.

14:14.730 --> 14:17.280
Only a few men are capable
of handling the role.

14:17.280 --> 14:18.710
They're not going to let him go.

14:19.190 --> 14:23.130
I heard that two of his
friends became monks in Aizu.

14:23.630 --> 14:27.960
He's probably begun to feel that
working so hard is meaningless.

14:31.980 --> 14:33.610
Oh, Yukinari.

14:34.540 --> 14:35.260
Yes?

14:35.750 --> 14:38.480
Have you heard about Sei Shonagon?

14:39.220 --> 14:42.570
No, I only know that she left

14:42.570 --> 14:44.800
the palace after Teishi-sama's death.

14:45.200 --> 14:46.280
Is that so?

14:46.750 --> 14:47.490
Yes.

14:47.820 --> 14:50.980
I've been keeping in touch with her.

14:50.980 --> 14:54.410
It appears that she'll be
leaving for Settsu very soon.

14:56.560 --> 14:58.280
I see...

14:59.610 --> 15:01.740
Why are you telling me this now?

15:01.740 --> 15:03.480
Weren't you friends?

15:04.390 --> 15:09.540
I wasn't sure if I should
tell you, but now you know.

15:10.060 --> 15:12.390
Thank you for your concern.

15:13.410 --> 15:15.380
Shonagon is leaving the capital...

15:16.480 --> 15:18.490
Without saying a word to me.

15:20.680 --> 15:24.360
Ever since Shoshi-sama
was named Empress,

15:24.360 --> 15:26.480
I've avoided her because I felt guilty.

15:29.640 --> 15:32.850
I'm no better than Tadanobu-sama.

15:32.850 --> 15:34.380
Then give it a try.

15:35.380 --> 15:39.340
Your earnest affection may do the trick.

15:39.830 --> 15:46.490
It's very difficult to overcome
barriers and keep love strong.

15:49.290 --> 15:52.760
I feel so tired...

16:10.380 --> 16:12.420
So you are easy.

16:14.610 --> 16:16.200
It's been a while.

16:17.110 --> 16:18.970
Was that you?

16:18.970 --> 16:19.580
Yes.

16:21.090 --> 16:23.780
Do you need something, Yukinari-sama?

16:23.780 --> 16:27.340
I was hoping to open the
gates of love tonight.

16:27.840 --> 16:29.190
Are you drunk?

16:29.190 --> 16:31.870
How rude.  That was an earnest joke.

16:31.870 --> 16:33.270
A joke?

16:33.270 --> 16:35.610
Why did you come here at this late hour?

16:35.610 --> 16:36.550
To joke.

16:37.400 --> 16:39.190
Since the gates will never open,

16:39.190 --> 16:41.480
can we at least talk tonight?

16:43.110 --> 16:44.400
The way we used to...

16:47.970 --> 16:50.170
Do you hate me?

16:51.510 --> 16:52.820
I don't.

16:53.890 --> 16:56.030
I have a general understanding

16:56.030 --> 16:58.700
of the inner workings of male politics.

16:59.260 --> 17:02.200
The government would stop
running if the Emperor

17:02.200 --> 17:04.380
and Michinaga-sama were at odds.

17:04.380 --> 17:08.290
Shoshi-sama's elevation was
necessary to facilitate that.

17:08.730 --> 17:12.670
You did the right thing
for this country.

17:13.740 --> 17:15.380
You fulfilled your role.

17:15.960 --> 17:17.140
Do you think so?

17:19.680 --> 17:22.070
If you still feel guilty,

17:22.070 --> 17:25.890
you could help look after
Teishi-sama's children.

17:26.680 --> 17:28.360
What about you?

17:29.050 --> 17:30.860
I heard that you will
be leaving the capital.

17:32.510 --> 17:33.290
Yes.

17:34.030 --> 17:36.690
You don't wish to serve
anyone besides Teishi-sama?

17:37.840 --> 17:41.130
You could stay in the palace
and look after her children.

17:41.850 --> 17:45.310
Michinaga-sama invited
you to serve again.

17:47.010 --> 17:49.820
As Teishi-sama's first lady-in-waiting,

17:49.820 --> 17:53.260
you will be scrutinized at first,

17:53.820 --> 17:57.630
but I promise to protect you!

17:59.340 --> 18:01.180
I appreciate your concern,

18:02.000 --> 18:03.730
but I have no intention of staying.

18:05.460 --> 18:07.880
I'm worried about
Teishi-sama's children,

18:07.880 --> 18:10.000
but I have another job to do.

18:11.150 --> 18:14.610
Do you remember what this is?

18:14.600 --> 18:17.950
The Pillow Book

18:15.040 --> 18:16.380
The Pillow Book.

18:16.980 --> 18:20.980
This doesn't mention any
of the sad events

18:20.980 --> 18:23.490
like the fall of their family
and Teishi-sama's death.

18:25.090 --> 18:28.410
I want future generations
to remember Teishi-sama

18:28.410 --> 18:32.280
for her bright, intelligent smile.

18:33.680 --> 18:36.130
It's my duty as Sei Shonagon

18:36.130 --> 18:39.430
to memorialize the time we
shared in The Pillow Book.

18:39.920 --> 18:44.310
That story wouldn't make sense if her

18:44.310 --> 18:48.350
most loyal servant went
on to serve someone else.

18:49.310 --> 18:52.290
I must step down from the stage,

18:52.790 --> 18:55.250
for my duty isn't over yet.

18:55.840 --> 18:57.090
I don't believe it...

18:57.690 --> 19:00.900
You're choosing your job
over her children...

19:00.900 --> 19:03.490
Both of us put our jobs first.

19:04.260 --> 19:05.330
You've got that right.

19:09.380 --> 19:11.430
Shonagon,

19:12.160 --> 19:14.880
the best moments of my life were when

19:14.880 --> 19:16.420
you and I talked about nothing.

19:17.990 --> 19:19.340
You wish to return to those days?

19:19.670 --> 19:20.590
Never.

19:21.210 --> 19:25.120
I'm not going to dwell on the past.

19:27.030 --> 19:28.310
Of course.

20:15.030 --> 20:17.710
I enjoyed our time
together, Yukinari-sama,

20:18.370 --> 20:20.610
but it's time to move on.

20:21.310 --> 20:25.780
Good memories are not meant
to tie you to the past.

20:26.340 --> 20:29.610
They serve to push you forward.

20:31.520 --> 20:35.000
We must try our best to move on,

20:35.750 --> 20:40.380
so we don't feel sad when
remembering the past

20:40.380 --> 20:42.780
and live full lives.

20:44.720 --> 20:47.480
We are currently in a
sorrowful winter of parting,

20:47.480 --> 20:50.140
but the snow will eventually
melt, and spring will come.

20:52.730 --> 21:01.490
And then, the feelings
we had will bloom again.

21:06.490 --> 21:09.950
Fujiwara no Yukinari went on to

21:09.950 --> 21:12.360
serve Prince Atsuyasu, son of Teishi,

21:12.360 --> 21:15.830
and he continued to hold that
post until the prince's death.

21:17.130 --> 21:22.010
Sei Shonagon's Pillow Book is
still spoken of to this day.

21:24.050 --> 21:27.020
Nights of love unforgotten

21:27.020 --> 21:31.760
in mourning tears of a curious hue.

21:32.900 --> 21:36.180
If you still remember
the love we shared,

21:36.180 --> 21:41.950
you will shed tears of
sorrow after I am gone.

21:41.950 --> 21:43.730
I wish to know their color.

21:46.300 --> 21:47.970
This was a sad poem written by Teishi

21:47.970 --> 21:50.550
in her later years, reflecting her loneliness.

21:51.040 --> 21:54.120
Teika did not include this
poem in the Hyakunin Isshu.

21:56.540 --> 22:00.340
The Sankanbon, the first
manuscript of the Pillow Book,

22:00.340 --> 22:02.560
is said to have been completed by Teika.

22:03.440 --> 22:06.020
Did Teika realize something

22:06.020 --> 22:08.720
as he was copying the Pillow Book?

22:07.220 --> 22:09.180
The Pillow Book (1)

22:09.470 --> 22:12.840
But because Teishi's poem was excluded

22:12.840 --> 22:15.390
from the famous Hyakunin Isshu,

22:15.390 --> 22:22.740
the name Empress Teishi immediately
invokes the Pillow Book.

22:23.970 --> 22:27.790
I want future generations
to remember Teishi-sama

22:27.790 --> 22:31.810
for her bright, intelligent smile.

22:33.010 --> 22:34.990
Poetic Tale 10:

22:33.010 --> 22:34.990
END

24:05.000 --> 25:00.000
Next
Episode

24:05.000 --> 25:00.000
Kaoriko and Fujiko

24:05.000 --> 25:00.000
Lady Murasaki

24:07.750 --> 24:12.620
Long last we meet, only
for me to leave hurriedly,

24:13.320 --> 24:15.450
for I could not recognize you,

24:15.450 --> 24:17.250
like the moon hidden behind the clouds.
